d": "XOM_10Q_2022-03-31__mdna__0035", "ticker": "XOM", "form": "10-Q", "fiscal_label": "Q1 FY2022", "period_end": "2022-03-31", "section": "mdna", "score": 0.894, "filing_name": "Exxon Mobil Corporation 10-Q Q1 FY2022", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/34088/000003408822000026/xom-20220331.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "XOM_10Q_2022-03-31__mdna__0034", "ticker": "XOM", "form": "10-Q", "fiscal_label": "Q1 FY2022", "period_end": "2022-03-31", "section": "mdna", "score": 0.8387, "filing_name": "Exxon Mobil Corporation 10-Q Q1 FY2022", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/34088/000003408822000026/xom-20220331.htm", "truncated": false}], "collapsed_near_duplicates": 21, "dropped_candidates": 130, "token_estimate": 31914, "gaps": [], "degraded": []}, "answer": {"direct_answer": "Exxon describes its market risk exposure first as commodity-price exposure: its businesses are \"fundamentally commodity businesses,\" so earnings may be significantly affected by oil, gas, and petrochemical prices and refining margins [XOM_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0001]. A material price decline could hurt especially Upstream, while a material increase could hurt Energy Products, Chemical Products, and Specialty Products [XOM_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0001]. The FY2025 10-K (period ended December 31, 2025) also names \"other market factors\": interest rates, inflation, currency exchange rates, and changes in usage of the U.S. dollar in global trade, plus possible losses from commodity derivatives and hedging or trading instruments, and it points to Item 7A for more [XOM_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0006]. Its 10-Qs (for example Q3 FY2025, ended September 30, 2025) state that market risk information does not differ materially from Item 7A of the prior 10-K [XOM_10Q_2025-09-30__mdna__0048]. The Item 7A text itself is not in the provided context.", "company_findings": [{"ticker": "XOM", "company": "Exxon Mobil Corporation", "findings": [{"point":